+---
+id: dl-008-cancelling-a-booking-refunds-the-full-total-only-before-it-starts
+type: decision-log
+title: "Cancelling a booking refunds the full total only before it starts"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+Customers ask to cancel bookings when plans change. `cancel(bookingId, at)` returns `{ bookingId, refund }`,
+the amount given back, and the brief does not say how much that is. The time `at` is passed in, so the
+refund may depend on when the cancellation happens. Totals are integer euro cents (dl-002), and an
+hourly or discounted total (dl-006, dl-007) is already the price the customer paid.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `cancel(bookingId, at)` refunds the booking's full `total` when `at` is strictly before the booking's
+  `start`.
+- When `at` is at or after `start`, the refund is `0`. The booking is still cancelled, so it releases its
+  equipment, and the customer gets nothing back.
+- `at` is validated as a UTC ISO-8601 instant, `YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ` with optional `.000` milliseconds, and
+  names an existing calendar day. Anything else throws, naming `at`.
+- A cancelled booking no longer holds its equipment: `book` and `availability` treat its period as free.
+- An unknown `bookingId` throws. A booking can be cancelled only once; a second cancel throws.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- A refund is always a whole number of cents, the stored `total` or `0`, so no rounding is needed.
+- The refund does not depend on the booking's price or discount, only on whether `at` is before `start`.
+  A partial refund schedule, such as a fee before the start, would be a new decision.
+- Cancelling after the start keeps the booking's record, with refund `0`. Cancelling after the end is
+  allowed and also refunds `0`; refusing it would be a separate decision.
+- `quote` keeps its behaviour from dl-004: it prices a period regardless of cancelled bookings.
